# Line endings are stored and checked out as LF, everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF in the working tree while git
# stores LF. Every commit warned about it, and — the part that actually cost
# something — a local `vite build` hashed CRLF bytes while CI hashed LF ones,
# so the same commit produced different bundle hashes in the two places. That
# made "compare the local hash to the deployed one" a useless way to check
# whether a deploy had landed, which is exactly how it was being used.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
